WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.848
Posts about travel, products in a catalog:

00:00:03.848 --> 00:00:06.400
almost every site groups its content.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.741
The Taxonomies module gives you managed categories and tags, linked to your content.

00:00:11.741 --> 00:00:17.200
This video covers how they are organized, chosen in the editor, and shown on the site.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.063
Without a shared list, every editor types categories by hand.

00:00:26.063 --> 00:00:29.626
One writes Travel, another Travels, a third Trips.

00:00:29.626 --> 00:00:35.670
Visitors can't follow a topic across the site, and one topic ends up under several names.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.904
A taxonomy is a managed vocabulary.

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:43.327
It holds terms, like Travel or Food, and the terms are organized as

00:00:43.327 --> 00:00:46.720
a hierarchy, with child terms under a parent term.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.835
A Taxonomy Field attaches terms to your content items.

00:00:50.835 --> 00:00:55.042
Editors pick terms from the list instead of typing them, and the site

00:00:55.042 --> 00:00:57.790
can show every item that belongs to a term.

00:01:01.996 --> 00:01:05.044
The Taxonomies module has two features.

00:01:05.044 --> 00:01:11.546
Let's open Tools, then Features, and type taxonomies in the Search box to filter the list.

00:01:12.003 --> 00:01:16.386
Taxonomies is the core feature, in the Content Management category.

00:01:16.386 --> 00:01:21.129
It provides the Taxonomy content type, the terms, and the Taxonomy Field.

00:01:21.129 --> 00:01:26.353
A site set up with the Blog recipe has it enabled; otherwise, you enable it here.

00:01:26.808 --> 00:01:30.337
Taxonomies Contents List Filters is optional.

00:01:30.337 --> 00:01:36.288
It adds filters by term to the Content Items list, and it depends on Taxonomies.

00:01:40.488 --> 00:01:44.509
A taxonomy is a content item of the Taxonomy type, so it is

00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:47.107
listed under Content, Content Items.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:53.108
Filtered by that type, the list shows the two taxonomies of this site, Categories and Tags.

00:01:53.563 --> 00:01:55.235
Let's edit Categories.

00:01:55.235 --> 00:01:59.655
Term Content Type sets the content type of the terms, here Category.

00:01:59.655 --> 00:02:02.463
Each term is a content item of that type.

00:02:02.932 --> 00:02:05.614
Below it is the hierarchy of terms.

00:02:05.614 --> 00:02:11.436
Travel is a term, and Food is a term with two child terms, Recipes and Restaurants.

00:02:11.436 --> 00:02:14.642
Each row has Edit, Add, and Delete buttons.

00:02:15.155 --> 00:02:18.190
Add Category creates a term at the top level.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:21.761
The Add button of a row creates a child term under it.

00:02:21.761 --> 00:02:27.535
The terms are stored inside the taxonomy, so you publish the taxonomy to publish its terms.

00:02:31.783 --> 00:02:34.472
Content is categorized with fields.

00:02:34.472 --> 00:02:36.374
Let's edit a Blog Post.

00:02:36.374 --> 00:02:40.309
Below the body, it has two fields that use taxonomies:

00:02:40.309 --> 00:02:41.883
Tags and Category.

00:02:42.336 --> 00:02:46.919
Category accepts one term, and only a term without children.

00:02:46.919 --> 00:02:48.655
Travel is selected.

00:02:48.655 --> 00:02:54.696
Food is a parent, so it is disabled, while Recipes and Restaurants can be chosen.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.085
Tags accepts several terms.

00:02:57.085 --> 00:03:01.735
Clicking the box lists the existing tags, and you select the ones you want.

00:03:01.735 --> 00:03:06.040
If you type a name that does not exist, pressing Enter creates a tag.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:10.880
When the post is published, the terms you selected are saved with it.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.260
Because editors choose from the list, every post uses the same names.

00:03:19.496 --> 00:03:25.142
On the site, the theme shows the category and the tags of each post as badges.

00:03:25.142 --> 00:03:27.966
Each badge is a link to a term page.

00:03:28.428 --> 00:03:32.815
The Travel page lists the content categorized with Travel, newest first.

00:03:32.815 --> 00:03:35.458
Here it shows the two posts about travel.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:40.937
Term pages are available when a taxonomy has Route contained items checked in

00:03:40.937 --> 00:03:44.207
its editor, and the theme decides how they look.

00:03:44.207 --> 00:03:46.690
A separate video covers term pages.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:56.142
You add a Taxonomy Field to a content part under Design, Content Definition.

00:03:56.142 --> 00:04:01.650
Its settings choose the taxonomy, and include Required, Unique, and Leaves only.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:06.390
The Tags editor has an Open setting for creating tags while editing.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:14.144
With Taxonomies Contents List Filters enabled, Settings, Taxonomy Filters chooses the taxonomies that

00:04:14.144 --> 00:04:16.500
filter the Content Items list.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:22.098
The Manage taxonomies permission controls who can add, edit, and delete terms.

00:04:22.098 --> 00:04:24.810
The Administrator role has it by default.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.191
That's Taxonomies:

00:04:28.191 --> 00:04:33.254
managed categories and tags for your content, with terms organized as a hierarchy.

00:04:33.254 --> 00:04:34.750
Thanks for watching.

